{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-30T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off the coast of Santa Catarina, a state in southern Brazil, the image captures a familiar ritual: surfers waiting beyond the breaking waves, their boards rising and falling with the Atlantic. From above, almost nothing seems to happen. But that's when the real work begins.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-CA1161995702_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-CA1161995702_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Reading between the waves","Title":"Aerial view of surfers, Santa Catarina, Brazil","Copyright":"© Wonderful Nature/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-27.374188,-48.654926/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-27.374188,-48.654926;S9;Santa Catarina, Brazil&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260829_SantaCatarina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brazil+Santa+Catarina&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260829_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260829_SantaCatarina"},"Ssd":"20260829","Name":"SantaCatarina","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1161995702","FullDateString":"Aug 29, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At sunset, Mont-Saint Michel rises from the waters of Normandy, France, like a fortress shaped by the sea. Perched on a rocky tidal island, the abbey and village stand at the centre of one of Europe's most dramatic coastal settings. Twice a day, the sea retreats to reveal vast stretches of sand before surging back to reclaim the landscape. At high tide, the mount becomes an island once again. For centuries, travellers timed their journeys to this rhythm, crossing the flats when conditions allowed and watching the sea return hours later.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-CA0604318625_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-CA0604318625_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where tides shape a legend","Title":"Mont-Saint-Michel during high tide, Manche, Normandy, France","Copyright":"© Clement LEONARD/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.637417,-1.5112/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.637417,-1.5112;S9;Mont-Saint-Michel, Normandy, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mont+Saint+Michel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260828_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset"},"Ssd":"20260828","Name":"MichelSunset","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"0604318625","FullDateString":"Aug 28, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine a world without the natural wonders that contain about 90% of Earth's surface freshwater. Lakes provide drinking water, support wildlife, help regulate climate and sustain communities around the globe. In recognition of their vital role, the United Nations designated 27 August as World Lake Day, first observed in 2025. The observance has particular relevance for Canadians, as Canada is home to more than two million lakes that shape its landscapes, ecosystems, recreation and freshwater resources. Protecting them is increasingly important as pollution, overuse and climate change put pressure on many lake environments.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-CA0091651040_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-CA0091651040_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Water, wildlife and wonder","Title":"Lesser flamingo flock at sunrise, Lake Magadi, Kenya","Copyright":"© Denis-Huot/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-1.902409,36.265224/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-1.902409,36.265224;S9;Lake Magadi, Kenya&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Lake+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260827_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi"},"Ssd":"20260827","Name":"LakeMagadi","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"0091651040","FullDateString":"Aug 27, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As darker nights return to Iceland, visitors will soon look to the skies for a chance to see the aurora borealis. Better known as the northern lights, this luminous phenomenon occurs when particles from the sun interact with gases high in Earth's atmosphere, creating shimmering ribbons of green, pink, purple and sometimes red light. Iceland's northern location and increasingly dark autumn and winter nights make it one of the world's premier destinations for aurora viewing.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-CA9381288782_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-CA9381288782_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A sky alive with colour","Title":"Auroras over Kirkjufell, Iceland","Copyright":"© Cavan Images/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/64.939949,-23.307478/3?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=64.939949,-23.307478;S9;Kirkjufell, Iceland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Aurora+borealis&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260826_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland"},"Ssd":"20260826","Name":"AurorasIceland","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9381288782","FullDateString":"Aug 26, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As morning breaks over Elliston, a small seabird appears with a wild iris held across its bill. The scene looks almost like a gift, yet biologists say Atlantic puffins are not known to offer flowers to their mates during courtship. The colourful bill, which becomes brightest in the breeding season and fades later in the year, helps make the photograph memorable. Even their feet turn brighter.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PurplePuffin_EN-CA8959604660_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PurplePuffin_EN-CA8959604660_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Clifftop flower carrier","Title":"Atlantic puffin holding a wild iris in his beak in Elliston, Newfoundland","Copyright":"© mlorenzphotography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.652341,-53.045912/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.652341,-53.045912;S9;Eliston, Newfoundland and Labrador&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260825_PurplePuffin\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Atlantic+puffin&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260825_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260825_PurplePuffin"},"Ssd":"20260825","Name":"PurplePuffin","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"8959604660","FullDateString":"Aug 25, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Brooklyn Bridge doesn't just connect Manhattan and Brooklyn—it bridges history, engineering and a few surprising stories too. Opened in 1883 after 14 years of construction, it became the world's first steel-wire suspension bridge, forever changing the way New Yorkers crossed the East River.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_EN-CA9847334652_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_EN-CA9847334652_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Crossing into history","Title":"Brooklyn Bridge, New York City, United States","Copyright":"© shayes17/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/40.706376,-73.996938/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=40.706376,-73.996938;S9;Brooklyn Bridge, New York City, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260824_BKBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brooklyn+Bridge&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260824_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260824_BKBridge"},"Ssd":"20260824","Name":"BKBridge","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9847334652","FullDateString":"Aug 24, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Alaska, some of the world's wildest wildlife spectacles unfold far from cities and roads. At Katmai National Park, brown bears line the river, and when the salmon jump, the show begins. Created in 1918 after the dramatic 1912 Novarupta volcanic eruption, the park protects more than 16,000 square kilometres of wilderness, including active volcanoes, tundra and salmon-rich rivers.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_EN-CA7184475938_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_EN-CA7184475938_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Meet Katmai's fishing giants","Title":"Brown bear fishing in river, Katmai National Park, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© Pal Hermansen/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/58.585845,-154.920897/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=58.585845,-154.920897;S9;Katmai National Park, Alaska, USA&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Katmai+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260823_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear"},"Ssd":"20260823","Name":"KatmaiBear","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"7184475938","FullDateString":"Aug 23, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When it comes to aerial acrobatics, hummingbirds are in a league of their own. Found only in the Americas, these tiny birds can hover in place, fly backwards and beat their wings dozens of times per second. As they visit flowers in search of nectar, they also serve as important pollinators, helping sustain ecosystems from alpine meadows to tropical rainforests. Their shimmering plumage, remarkable agility and high-energy lifestyles make them some of the world's most fascinating birds.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_EN-CA4098383254_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_EN-CA4098383254_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Small birds, big impact","Title":"Green-crowned brilliant hummingbirds feeding on lobster-claw flowers, Costa Rica","Copyright":"© Paul Hobson/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"With the highest metabolic rate of any vertebrate, hummingbirds may need to feed every 10 minutes.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Green-crowned+brilliant&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260905_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned"},"Ssd":"20260905","Name":"GreenCrowned","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"4098383254","FullDateString":"Sep 5, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Rising above the salt marshes along Germany's North Sea coast, the Westerheversand Lighthouse is instantly recognisable thanks to its distinctive red-and-white stripes. Built between 1906 and 1908, the lighthouse has stood as an icon on the Eiderstedt Peninsula for more than a century, guiding ships through the waters of the North Sea. Today, it remains one of northern Germany's best-known coastal landmarks. Visitors who climb its 157 steps are rewarded with sweeping views of the surrounding scenery.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_EN-CA7107631944_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_EN-CA7107631944_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Red and white on the horizon","Title":"Westerheversand Lighthouse in Westerhever, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany","Copyright":"© bluejayphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/54.373402,8.6399/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=54.373402,8.6399;S9;Westerheversand Lighthouse, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Westerheversand+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260904_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand"},"Ssd":"20260904","Name":"Westerheversand","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"7107631944","FullDateString":"Sep 4, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some mountain roads become destinations in their own right, and Julier Pass is one of them. This Swiss mountain pass rises to 2,284 metres and has linked Alpine valleys along a route used for nearly 2,000 years. Its story began long before modern traffic. No guardrails, no pavement—just a route used by Roman travellers, merchants and messengers. Archaeological finds near the summit, including countless coins and two Roman soapstone columns, suggest there was once a sanctuary or stopping place for those tackling the climb.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JulierPass_EN-CA1672226611_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JulierPass_EN-CA1672226611_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The climb is calling","Title":"Winding road of Julier Pass, Switzerland","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/46.471172,9.725359/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=46.471172,9.725359;S9;Julier Pass, Switzerland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260903_JulierPass\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Julier+Pass+Switzerland&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260903_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260903_JulierPass"},"Ssd":"20260903","Name":"JulierPass","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1672226611","FullDateString":"Sep 3, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Along England's east shore, the Suffolk Heritage Coast blends windswept heaths, marshes, shingle beaches and expansive North Sea views. One of its best-known towns is Southwold, where water and history are inseparable. Almost encircled by the sea, the River Blyth and surrounding wetlands, the town occupies a slender peninsula shaped by centuries of fishing, trade and life at the edge of the water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_EN-CA7283935954_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_EN-CA7283935954_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Painted along the shore","Title":"Traditional beach huts, Southwold, Suffolk Heritage Coast, England","Copyright":"© stevendocwra/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/52.326221,1.678968/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=52.326221,1.678968;S9;Southwold, Suffolk, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Southwold+Suffolk&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260902_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts"},"Ssd":"20260902","Name":"SuffolkHuts","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"7283935954","FullDateString":"Sep 2, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Fungi often go unnoticed beneath forest floors, lawns and fallen leaves, yet their underground threads help recycle nutrients and support healthy ecosystems. The mushrooms we see are only the fruiting bodies of much larger organisms. They appear briefly, release spores, then disappear from sight. Unlike plants, fungi belong to a kingdom of their own. Some species even glow, while others form partnerships with trees.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_EN-CA6859526783_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_EN-CA6859526783_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A world beneath your feet","Title":"Horsehair parachute fungus, Belarus","Copyright":"© Máté/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"In southeastern Pennsylvania, Kennett Square has earned a global reputation as the 'Mushroom Capital of the World.'","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Fungus&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260901_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom"},"Ssd":"20260901","Name":"HorseHairShroom","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6859526783","FullDateString":"Sep 1, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Stand in Registan Square and it's easy to see why it is considered the architectural heart of Samarkand—one of Central Asia's oldest cities. This plaza in Uzbekistan is framed by three magnificent madrasas—Islamic centres of learning—whose soaring portals draw the eye upward. Yet some of the square's greatest treasures reveal themselves only when you look closer.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-CA1921310723_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-CA1921310723_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A master class in pattern","Title":"Building detail of Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan","Copyright":"© Piero M. Bianchi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/39.655009,66.975755/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=39.655009,66.975755;S9;Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Samarkand&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260831_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling"},"Ssd":"20260831","Name":"SamarkandCeiling","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1921310723","FullDateString":"Aug 31, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today, International Whale Shark Day makes room for the world's largest fish. Despite their name, whale sharks are not whales but fish, reaching lengths of up to 18 metres and weighing around 18 metric tonnes. Found in warm tropical seas, they glide through the water with their mouths open, filtering plankton, fish eggs and other tiny prey. This species' distinctive white-spot patterns are unique to each individual, much like human fingerprints.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-CA1504942162_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-CA1504942162_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The fish that outgrew its name","Title":"Whale shark and golden trevally, Cenderawasih Bay, West Papua, Indonesia","Copyright":"© Pete Oxford/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Whale sh